<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'">
  <title>S073 — Cache loss and required profile recovery</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer=""></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer=""></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#controls">Skip to operator controls</a>
  <header>
    <p class="banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S073: Cache access lost</h1>
    <p>Recover the required synthetic profile within the declared budget. A quick empty object is never a successful fallback.</p>
    <p>A-S073 · D-S073 · SC-S073 · frozen S · one local learning unit</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <section aria-labelledby="contract-title">
      <h2 id="contract-title">Declare the recovery contract</h2>
      <p><strong>Required state:</strong> synthetic-profile-073, revision 7, label “Sample learner 073”, dark theme, saved items synthetic-item-1 and synthetic-item-2. Every field must remain intact.</p>
      <p><strong>Preconditions:</strong> one fixed, entirely fictional profile and one deterministic attempt at a time. Cache success costs 10 synthetic ms. Observed cache loss costs 20 ms; durable recovery adds 90 ms (110 ms total). Equality to the budget is permitted.</p>
      <p>SUCCESS means known correct state within budget. FAILURE includes missing, wrong, stale, unavailable or over-budget state. UNKNOWN means the observation is missing, never a successful recovery. A known missed budget is still FAILURE if state is unknown.</p>
      <p>Choose controls, run once, inspect the trace, predict the classification, then check. Checking tests your reasoning; it cannot change the measured result.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="controls-title" id="controls">
      <h2 id="controls-title">Operator controls</h2>
      <p id="phase" role="status">Phase: checked</p>
      <form id="attempt-form" novalidate="">
        <fieldset id="configuration" disabled="">
          <legend>Configure one synthetic attempt</legend>
          <label for="cache">Cache observation</label>
          <select id="cache" name="cache">
            <option value="lost" selected="">Cache access lost</option>
            <option value="available">Known correct cache read (baseline)</option>
            <option value="unknown">Cache observation missing</option>
          </select>
          <label for="recovery">When cache access is lost</label>
          <select id="recovery" name="recovery">
            <option value="durable" selected="">Use durable recovery receipt</option>
            <option value="empty">Substitute an empty profile (unsafe comparison)</option>
            <option value="fail">Return explicit failure</option>
          </select>
          <label for="durable">Synthetic durable receipt</label>
          <select id="durable" name="durable">
            <option value="correct" selected="">Exact required profile, revision 7</option>
            <option value="stale">Stale profile, revision 6</option>
            <option value="wrong">Different synthetic profile ID</option>
            <option value="empty">Empty profile {}</option>
            <option value="unavailable">Explicitly unavailable</option>
            <option value="unknown">Returned-profile receipt missing</option>
          </select>
          <label for="budget">Total journey budget (synthetic ms)</label>
          <select id="budget" name="budget">
            <option value="80">80 — durable path is too slow</option>
            <option value="110">110 — exact durable boundary</option>
            <option value="150" selected="">150 — durable path fits</option>
          </select>
        </fieldset>
        <button id="run-attempt" type="submit" disabled="">Run synthetic attempt</button>
      </form>
      <p id="input-error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden=""></p>
      <form id="check-form" novalidate="">
        <fieldset id="prediction-controls" disabled="">
          <legend>Inspect the result, then check your prediction</legend>
          <label for="prediction">Classification prediction</label>
          <select id="prediction" name="prediction" aria-describedby="prediction-result">
            <option value="" selected="">Choose a classification</option>
            <option value="SUCCESS">SUCCESS</option>
            <option value="FAILURE">FAILURE</option>
            <option value="UNKNOWN">UNKNOWN</option>
          </select>
          <button id="check-result" type="submit">Check prediction</button>
        </fieldset>
      </form>
      <p id="prediction-result" role="status">Prediction incorrect; actual result remains FAILURE.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <button id="new-attempt" type="button">New attempt (retain history)</button>
        <button id="reset-rehearsal" type="button" aria-describedby="reset-help">Reset rehearsal and history</button>
      </div>
      <p id="reset-help">Reset deliberately clears all six local attempt slots, traces, predictions and errors. It restores defaults and focus; no live or durable state is touched.</p>
      <p id="history-count">Retained attempts: 1 / 6</p>
      <p>Use Tab, arrow keys, Enter and Space for the controls. Attempts are locked after running; check before starting another. At six attempts, reset is required.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="outcome-title">
      <h2 id="outcome-title">Observed synthetic result</h2>
      <p id="outcome" role="status" aria-live="polite">FAILURE — EMPTY_PROFILE</p>
      <p id="metrics">Elapsed: 20 synthetic ms; budget: 150 ms; required state: invalid.</p>
      <p id="detail">An empty object is not the required profile, even when returned quickly.</p>
      <h3>Returned profile observation</h3>
      <pre id="profile">{}</pre>
      <h3>Deterministic trace</h3>
      <ol id="trace"><li>20 ms | cache | Cache access lost; no cached profile returned.</li><li>20 ms | empty substitute | An empty object was substituted: required state is missing.</li><li>20 ms | assertion | FAILURE: EMPTY_PROFILE. An empty object is not the required profile, even when returned quickly.</li></ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="history-title">
      <h2 id="history-title">Retained attempt history</h2>
      <p id="totals">Measured attempts: 1; SUCCESS 0; FAILURE 1; UNKNOWN 0. All observed results counted; a learning check cannot change them.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <caption>All results, including unchecked, failed and unknown attempts, remain until explicit reset.</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Attempt</th><th scope="col">Configuration</th><th scope="col">Actual result</th><th scope="col">Timing / state</th><th scope="col">Learning check</th><th scope="col">Retained trace</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="history"><tr><td>1</td><td>cache=lost; recovery=empty; durable=correct; budget=150</td><td>FAILURE: EMPTY_PROFILE</td><td>20 / 150 ms; state=false</td><td>SUCCESS: incorrect</td><td><details><summary>Trace for attempt 1</summary><pre>20 ms | cache | Cache access lost; no cached profile returned.
20 ms | empty substitute | An empty object was substituted: required state is missing.
20 ms | assertion | FAILURE: EMPTY_PROFILE. An empty object is not the required profile, even when returned quickly.</pre></details></td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <h2 id="limits-title">Limits and native remainder</h2>
      <p>This finite model has no network, persistence, real identity, authentication, sessions or credentials. All profile IDs, contents, receipts and timings are synthetic; no Azure management API or cache service is called.</p>
      <p>A browser lesson pass is not actual cache-outage or durable-profile recovery certification, five-nines continuity evidence, production Node.js 24 support, or completion of B-S073 / D-S073. The native sibling still needs CORE, DATA, HOST and approved real recovery observations within budgets.</p>
      <p>Open this HTML file directly. Closing or reloading discards this page's memory. IaC, cloud resources, packages and deployment are not required or authorized.</p>
    </section>
  </main>


</body></html>